course: dictionary
lesson: 9849
title: Swot and the power of studying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A swot is a pupil who studies very hard. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people use it in everyday school talk. Look at the clues: «Stop being such a swot!» is said to someone who works hard, so it is often teasing.
explain: Swot can also be a verb: to swot or swot up means to study hard, especially before a test. «Swot up on your spellings before Friday» tells you to study before the test day. The word before is a clue that the studying comes first.
explain: Capital letters change the meaning. SWOT, written in capitals, is short for Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities and Threats. It is a way to plan or judge an idea, so it has nothing to do with studying. Check the context to find out which meaning you need.
fact: A swot is a pupil who studies very hard.
fact: To swot up means to study hard, especially before a test.
fact: Being called a swot for trying is common teasing, but working hard is a good thing.
fact: Other keen pupils are out there, so you do not need to stop trying because of teasing.
fact: SWOT stands for Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities and Threats.
exercise: «Stop being such a swot!» What is a swot in this sentence? | *A pupil who works very hard, said as teasing | A sleepy cat in the classroom | A fast runner on the sports field
exercise: «Swot up on your spellings before Friday.» What does swot up mean? | *To study hard, especially before a test | To lose your pencil | To play a game outside | To eat lunch quickly
exercise: In a business project, SWOT is an abbreviation. What do the letters stand for? | *Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats | Students, Work, Oral, Tests | Strong, Wild, Open, Tired
test: In the UK, which everyday word means a pupil who studies very hard? | Wanderer | *Swot | Champion | Dreamer
test: Which sentence uses swot up correctly? | Swot up is a bird that sings. | My swot up is a blue pencil. | *I need to swot up for my maths test. | I can swot up a sandwich at lunch.
exam: Which idea about being called a swot for trying hard is best? | It means you must never study | It means you should stop trying | *Working hard is good, even if some people tease you | It means you are a bad pupil
